        "type": "text/plain",
        "value": "<div data-rss-type=\"text\">\r\n  <h3>\r\n    <span>\r\n      <span>\r\n        \n            Executive Assistant to the Tumuaki -\n           \r\n      </span>\r\n    </span>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           CLOSED\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </h3>\r\n  <h5>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           \u014ctaki Campus\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </h5>\r\n  <h5>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           1.0\u00a0 FTE Full time, Fixed Term (6 months with potential to extend)\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </h5>\r\n  <h5>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           9am \u2013 5pm\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </h5>\r\n</div>\r\n<div data-rss-type=\"text\">\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           Are you after a dynamic role within a kaupapa M\u0101ori environment with opportunity to advance your career? A special and unique place of learning, Te W\u0101nanga o Raukawa is a tikanga M\u0101ori tertiary education provider. A vacancy has arisen for an Executive Assistant extraordinaire to join Te Whare o Te Tumuaki full time covering maternity leave at our main campus located in \u014ctaki.\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <br/>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           The successful applicant will be required to perform a variety of administrative tasks and provide support to the tumuaki, Dr Mereana Selby.\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      <span>\r\n        \n            Responsibilities include but are not limited to managing calendars, emails, minute taking, preparing travel arrangements and drafting or preparing relevant documentation and publications as required. Successful applicants should have a sound knowledge of the guiding kaupapa of Te W\u0101nanga o Raukawa, be highly organised, have time management skills, be able to take initiative, and have competency of te reo M\u0101ori.\u00a0\n           \r\n      </span>\r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <br/>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <a href=\"null\" target=\"_blank\">\r\n      \n           Applications close: Friday 17 March 2024\n          \r\n    </a>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <br/>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      <span>\r\n        \n            For a full job description, or to apply contact:\n           \r\n      </span>\r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           Dionne Seng, Kaihaut\u016b Te Whare Tiaki Rawa\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      <span>\r\n        \n            \u012am\u0113ra:\n           \r\n      </span>\r\n    </span>\r\n    <a href=\"mailto:dionne.seng@twor-otaki.ac.nz\" target=\"_blank\">\r\n      \n           dionne.seng@twor-otaki.ac.nz\n          \r\n    </a>\r\n    <span>\r\n      <span>\r\n      </span>\r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           Waea: 06 3649011 extn 757\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n</div>"
      }
